{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A vertex is discovered, then its out-edges are reported, then it is finished. An edge to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undiscovered vertex is a tree edge, and the search continues from that vertex before the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge. An edge to a vertex discovered but not yet finished is a back edge; a self-loop is one.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An edge to a finished vertex is a forward edge when that vertex was discovered later than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex being explored, and a cross edge otherwise.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a directed graph every out-edge of an explored vertex is reported. In an undirected graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each edge is reported once, from the end that reaches it first: the tree edge is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported again from the vertex it discovered, but a parallel edge to the parent is a back edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a self-loop is one back edge. Without pruning or a depth limit an undirected search has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only tree and back edges; an edge to a finished vertex whose edges were not explored is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forward or cross edge."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/backEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/crossEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/discover(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/finish(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/forwardEdge(_:)","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/treeEdge(_:)"]},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:9Traversal25EdgeDepthFirstSearchEventO","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"}],"symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/EdgeSearchEvents.swift#L37","fileName":"EdgeSearchEvents.swift"}},"relationshipsSect